cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AB Factory — corpus of A/B test interpretation errors"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Davydov
    given-names: Alexander
    website: "https://davydov.my"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzotop/ab-factory-demo"
url: "https://yzotop.github.io/ab-factory-demo/"
abstract: >-
  660 synthetic A/B experiment cases, each with exactly one interpretation
  error built into it — peeking, sample ratio mismatch, Simpson's paradox,
  heavy tails, bot traffic, logging defects and 27 others — together with a
  computed ground-truth verdict for every case. A deterministic policy rule
  scores 100% on a 100-case set covering five mechanisms and 42.7% on the
  full 660-case corpus covering 33; twenty of the thirty-three mechanisms it
  fails completely. Two documented properties constrain measurement on this
  corpus: 129 cases name their mechanism in plain text inside the contract,
  and in 66 cases the deciding evidence is absent from the results table.
keywords:
  - ab-testing
  - experimentation
  - synthetic-dataset
  - benchmark
  - statistical-errors
  - llm-evaluation
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
date-released: 2026-08-15
